3.5 Media representations
Students should have knowledge and understanding of how the media portray events, issues,
individuals and social groups.

Students will be required to demonstrate knowledge and understanding of how media products
reflect the social, cultural, historical and political contexts in which they are produced. Not every
question in every exam series will require the analysis of the four contexts but students will need to
be familiar with all of them in relation to a range of media products.

In the following table, the column headed Content includes the mandatory material which all
students should study. The column headed Guidance Notes includes pointers and suggestions to
help schools and colleges interpret and deliver the content where these are appropriate. These
Guidance Notes will be supplemented by further support materials (the CSP booklet).

